#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0333 expect=skipped domain=LBHM
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a Findings About dataset name begins with "FA", is longer than two characters, and the characters following "FA" do not match the two-character code of a domain present in the study.
#note "Verdict changed noViolation -> skipped on 2026-10-02: CDISC-CG0333 is now scoped to Findings About datasets only (Domains.Include: [FA] + include_split_datasets: true, owner). LBHM is a split of LB (DOMAIN LB), its data-derived base LB is not FA, so it is out of scope before the check is reached. Until then the rule was scoped to ALL splits and this scenario was the in-scope control for the FA-prefix conjunct."
dataset LBHM label="Laboratory Test Results split by category"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1023
---

dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015
---
